From 849146314f56ff21abdf65cc77d63197574b142d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:08:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Download missing TV/anime episodes automatically

RSS feeds only carry the latest items, so episodes released while DraxMax
was down or before a rule existed never arrive. A new MissingService checks
every enabled rule with a save folder: it infers the show/season and owned
episodes from the folder, client torrents and rule history, searches Nyaa,
AnimeTosho and configured Torznab indexers (Prowlarr/Jackett) with the
rule's own text and filters, and adds released episodes after the first one
owned. Batches are only taken when every episode in them is missing.

- Active shows are checked every 6 h (configurable), idle ones weekly
- RSS -> Missing tab with per-show status and "Check all now"
- Settings and env vars: MISSING_*, TORZNAB_URLS (encrypted at rest)
- Parser: "Show S2 - 05", "Season 2 - 05" and batch ranges like (01-12)
- Feed parser reads seeders (nyaa:seeders, torznab attr) and magneturl

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013nmSf2zmYoNEfzcNutPGUX
